You are the Formatter skill. You are the conventional TERMINAL node of
every DAG. Your job is to produce the final user-facing answer from
whatever upstream nodes have provided.

You make no tool calls. The user's original query appears under
USER_QUERY. Upstream results appear under INPUTS.

Procedure:
  1. Read USER_QUERY.
  2. Read INPUTS and decide which fields / findings answer the query.
  3. Write the user-facing answer in plain English. Adapt the format
     (numbered list, comparison table, one paragraph) to what the
     question actually asked.

Output schema (JSON, no prose, no markdown fences):

  {
    "final_answer": "<the answer the user sees>"
  }

Rules:
  - This is the LAST node. Do not add successors.
  - The answer must be answerable from INPUTS alone. If an upstream
    node returned `(not found)` or marked itself failed, say so plainly
    to the user rather than inventing.
  - Cite sources only when an upstream node included them (Researcher
    nodes do; Retriever nodes do). Do not invent URLs.

USER_QUERY: Find the populations of London, Paris, Berlin and tell me which two are closest in size.

MEMORY HITS (2 from FAISS):
  - [tool_outcome] Fetch Claude Shannon wikipedia page for birth date, death date, and three information theory contributions
      source: user_query
      raw: Fetch https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Shannon and tell me his birth date, death date, and three key contributions to information theory.
  - [tool_outcome] Fetch Claude Shannon wikipedia page for birth date, death date, and three information theory contributions
      source: user_query
      raw: Fetch https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Shannon and tell me his birth date, death date, and three key contributions to information theory.

INPUTS:
[
  {
    "id": "USER_QUERY",
    "kind": "query",
    "value": "Find the populations of London, Paris, Berlin and tell me which two are closest in size."
  },
  {
    "id": "n:2",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the current population of London?",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://worldpopulationreview.com/cities/united-kingdom/london",
          "title": "London Population 2026"
        }
      ],
      "findings": "Estimates for the population of London vary depending on the source and the definition of the area (e.g., Greater London versus the wider metropolitan area). According to World Population Review's internal projections, the population of London is estimated at approximately 9.14 million for 2025 and 9.19 million for 2026.\n\nOther metrics, such as those from Macrotrends, provide higher estimates for the London metropolitan area, citing figures approaching 9.9 million for 2026. Official statistics from the UK's Office for National Statistics (ONS) typically rely on census data, which is conducted decennially, meaning recent figures are often projections based on previous census trends."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "n:3",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the current population of Paris?",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris",
          "title": "Paris - Wikipedia"
        }
      ],
      "findings": "The population of Paris is typically classified into the city proper and the broader metropolitan area. As of recent estimates, the population of the city proper is approximately 2.04 million people within its 105.4 square kilometer area.\n\nThe Paris metropolitan area is significantly larger, with a population estimated at approximately 13.2 million as of January 2026."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "n:4",
    "kind": "upstream",
    "skill": "researcher",
    "output": {
      "question": "What is the current population of Berlin?",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berlin",
          "title": "Berlin - Wikipedia"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.thegroundsag.com/en/2026/02/19/berlins-population-rose-to-more-than-3-9-million-in-2025/",
          "title": "Berlin's population rose to more than 3.9 million in 2025"
        }
      ],
      "findings": "As of December 31, 2025, the population of Berlin was recorded at 3,913,644 inhabitants according to the city's population register. \n\nPrior to this, data from the end of 2024 indicated that the city-state had approximately 3.897 million registered inhabitants. Berlin remains the most populous city proper within the European Union."
    }
  }
]
